{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nplan={\\\"description\\\":\\\"Discriminator: with recording enabled and the recovering replica's own row already holding a different instance at the same number, which record's metadata reaches the stable store when phase 1 starts for another replica's instance? Prefix: the harness seeds the own row with distinctive metadata (seq 0x33333333, status ACCEPTED) and calls the real startPhase1 for the owner's instance. Controls: the prerequisite prints the durability flag and the own row's seq and status, and the result prints the bytes written together with the recorded seq and status, the new instance's seq and the own row's seq.\\\",\n \\\"claim_id\\\":\\\"C9-durable-recorder-uses-the-instance-row\\\",\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB10-phase1-record\\\"],\n \\\"harness\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"go_test\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"In-package Go test that seeds the recovering replica's own row, runs the real phase-1 entry with recording enabled and decodes the metadata the recorder wrote.\\\",\n  \\\"semantic_changes\\\":[\\\"harness-only scaffolding: the Replica is constructed in-package with a harness temp stable store and startPhase1 is called directly with the owner's coordinates\\\",\\\"the own row is seeded with a synthetic instance so the two rows differ; protocol code is unmodified\\\"],\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"two_rows\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"durable_two_rows_prepared\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"durable\\\",\\\"value\\\":True}]}],\n  \\\"legality\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S8-handlePropose-startPhase1\\\",\\\"S19-durable-record\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB10-phase1-record\\\"],\n   \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"A replica can hold its own instance at a number while restarting phase 1 for another replica's instance of the same number, which is what the two rows represent.\\\",\\\"applicability\\\":\\\"Durable true, recovery-led phase 1, own row occupied.\\\",\\\"unresolved\\\":[\\\"the recorded bytes are decoded with the layout the recorder uses, not with a reader's layout (see claim C2)\\\"],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]}},\n \\\"monitors\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"M1-wrong-row-record\\\",\\\"checker_id\\\":\\\"CH2-wrong-row-record\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"durable_wrong_row_recorded\\\",\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB10-phase1-record\\\"],\n   \\\"grounding\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S8-handlePropose-startPhase1\\\",\\\"S19-durable-record\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB10-phase1-record\\\"],\n    \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"The event compares the metadata the recorder wrote with the two candidate records, which is the claim's question.\\\",\\\"applicability\\\":\\\"The own row held an instance and the new instance was installed under the owner's row.\\\",\\\"unresolved\\\":[],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"instance\\\",\\\"reference\\\":\\\"two_rows.instance\\\"}],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"two_rows\\\"}],\n \\\"observable_properties\\\":[{\\\"checker_id\\\":\\\"CH2-wrong-row-record\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"event_assertion\\\",\\\"trigger\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"event\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"durable_wrong_row_recorded\\\"},\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"recorded_matches_new_instance\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"instance\\\"],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"The metadata recorded for a phase-1 write must belong to the instance being written.\\\"}],\n \\\"uncertainties\\\":[\\\"the check relies on the recorder's own byte layout to decode what was written, which claim C2 shows is not readable as documented\\\",\\\"the durable path is inert in the shipped configuration\\\"]}\nsub={\\\"action\\\":\\\"check\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"unit-C9-durable-recorder-uses-the-instance-row\\\",\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Second scenario for the same obligation: when the recovering replica's own row already holds an instance at that number there is no panic, but the recorder writes that other instance's metadata. The harness seeds the own row with distinctive values and decodes what the real recorder wrote: the run shows recorded seq 858993459 equal to the own row's seq and not the new instance's, with the own row's ACCEPTED status, so the stable store receives a different instance's ballot context. The first artifact covered the panic case; this one covers the silent case, and the trusted runner plus a fresh correspondence review decide it.\\\",\n \\\"plan_path\\\":\\\"plan-wrong-row-record.json\\\",\\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"explore_durable_row2_test.go\\\",\\\"files\\\":{}}\njson.dump(plan,open('plan-wrong-row-record.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-wrong-row-record.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('written')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-wrong-row-record.json 2>&1 | head -8\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
